    <h2>Overall Security Level Assessment</h2>
    <p>The overall security level is determined by analyzing all discovered vulnerabilities and applying a weighted scoring system. The calculation follows these key principles:</p>

    <h3>Classification by CVSS Severity:</h3>
    <p>Each vulnerability is categorized according to its CVSS (Common Vulnerability Scoring System) rating, using the following severity levels:</p>
    <table>
        <tr>
            <th>Score</th>
            <th>Category</th>
            <th>Description</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>9.0 &lt; CVSS &lt; 10.0</td>
            <td><span class="sev-badge sev-critical">CRITICAL</span></td>
            <td>Critical risk on the information system requiring immediate correction or imposing an immediate shutdown of the service.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>7.0 &lt; CVSS &lt; 8.9</td>
            <td><span class="sev-badge sev-high">HIGH</span></td>
            <td>Major risk on the information system requiring a short-term correction.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>4.0 &lt; CVSS &lt; 6.9</td>
            <td><span class="sev-badge sev-medium">MEDIUM</span></td>
            <td>Moderate risk on the information system and requiring medium-term correction.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>0.1 &lt; CVSS &lt; 3.9</td>
            <td><span class="sev-badge sev-low">LOW</span></td>
            <td>Low risk on the information system and may require correction.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>CVSS = 0.0</td>
            <td><span class="sev-badge sev-info">INFORMATION</span></td>
            <td>General recommendations intended to advise on the security of the information system.</td>
        </tr>
    </table>

    <h3>Weighted Scoring Formula:</h3>
    <p>To reflect the significance of higher-severity vulnerabilities, each category is assigned a weight factor, and the overall security score is computed using the following formula:</p>
    <div class="formula-box">
        <p class="formula"><i>Weighted Score</i> = (C × 4) + (H × 3) + (M × 2) + (L × 1) / C + H + M + L</p>
    </div>
    <div class="formula-legend">
        <p>Where:</p>
        <table>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="sev-badge sev-critical">C</span></td>
                <td>Number of Critical vulnerabilities</td>
                <td><span class="sev-badge sev-medium">M</span></td>
                <td>Number of Medium vulnerabilities</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="sev-badge sev-high">H</span></td>
                <td>Number of High vulnerabilities</td>
                <td><span class="sev-badge sev-low">L</span></td>
                <td>Number of Low vulnerabilities</td>
            </tr>
        </table>
        <p class="text-muted" style="font-size: var(--z-11px); margin-top: var(--z-8px);">Informational findings (CVSS 0.0) are excluded from this calculation as they do not present immediate security risks.</p>
    </div>

    <h3>Mapping the Weighted Score to Security Levels:</h3>
    <p>The computed weighted score is then mapped to a qualitative security level, which provides a high-level assessment of the system's overall security posture:</p>
    <table>
        <tr>
            <th>Weighted Score</th>
            <th>Overall Security Level</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>3.5 - 4.0</td>
            <td><span class="sev-badge sev-critical">CRITICAL</span></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>2.5 - 3.4</td>
            <td><span class="sev-badge sev-high">HIGH</span></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>1.5 - 2.4</td>
            <td><span class="sev-badge sev-medium">MEDIUM</span></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>0.5 - 1.4</td>
            <td><span class="sev-badge sev-low">LOW</span></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>0 - 0.4</td>
            <td><span class="sev-badge sev-info">INFORMATIONAL</span></td>
        </tr>
    </table>

    <h2>Structure for Vulnerability Presentation</h2>
    <table class="vuln-structure-table">
        <tr>
            <td class="label-cell">Description</td>
            <td>Short description of the vulnerability.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td class="label-cell">Attack surface</td>
            <td>Specifies precisely the vulnerable element (IP, parameter, etc.).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td class="label-cell">Reference(s)</td>
            <td>Terminology attributed to the flaw (CVE, CWE or OWASP code, when relevant).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td class="label-cell">Severity</td>
            <td>
                <p>SERMA Safety &amp; Security use a <u>c</u>ommon <u>V</u>ulnerability <u>S</u>coring <u>S</u>ystem) in its latest version. This standard is developed by the FIRST (<b>F</b>orum of <b>I</b>ncident <b>R</b>esponse and <b>S</b>ecurity <b>T</b>eams) and is internationally recognized.</p>
                <div class="severity-level">
                    <span class="sev-badge sev-info">INFORMATION</span>: Score 0.0<br>
                    General recommendations not associated with vulnerabilities and intended to advise you on the security of your information system.
                </div>
                <div class="severity-level">
                    <span class="sev-badge sev-low">LOW</span>: Score between 0.1 and 3.9<br>
                    Low risk on the information system and may require correction.
                </div>
                <div class="severity-level">
                    <span class="sev-badge sev-medium">MEDIUM</span>: Score between 4.0 and 6.9<br>
                    Moderate risk on the information system and requiring medium-term correction.
                </div>
                <div class="severity-level">
                    <span class="sev-badge sev-high">HIGH</span>: Score between 7.0 and 8.9<br>
                    Major risk on the information system requiring a short-term correction.
                </div>
                <div class="severity-level">
                    <span class="sev-badge sev-critical">CRITICAL</span>: Score between 9.0 and 10.0<br>
                    Critical risk on the information system requiring immediate correction or imposing an immediate shutdown of the service.
                </div>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td class="label-cell">Impact(s)</td>
            <td>
                <p>Consequences of the vulnerability exploitation on your information system.</p>
                <div class="cia-triad">
                    <div class="cia-item">
                        <div class="cia-header">Confidentiality</div>
                        <div class="cia-icon">&#128065;</div>
                        <div class="cia-value cia-none">None</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="cia-item">
                        <div class="cia-header">Integrity</div>
                        <div class="cia-icon">&#9997;</div>
                        <div class="cia-value cia-low">Low</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="cia-item">
                        <div class="cia-header">Availability</div>
                        <div class="cia-icon">&#9881;</div>
                        <div class="cia-value cia-high">High</div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <p>Other impacts:<br>Financial, legal, reputation, business</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td class="label-cell">Remediation</td>
            <td>Solutions to resolve the vulnerability and improve the level of security temporarily or permanently.</td>
        </tr>
    </table>
    <p>Then follows elements of proof that the vulnerability exists (screenshots, scenarios, impacted URLs, etc.).</p>
</page>
